      "message": "Eric, if you have a chance, could you please provide early feedback on the interface, before I proceed to implementation.\n\nPlease note that I have considered non-blocking input as well, although currently we don\u0027t have corresponding flag at the HAL level (system/hardware/interfaces/media/aidl/android/media/audio/common/AudioInputFlags.aidl). However, this mode might make sense when buffers are large. In this case, the HAL unblocks the client from a read operation before the data is actually available, and notifies it via a callback when the data has been obtained.\n\nAlso note that when the h/w is not consuming (for output) or producing (for input), the I/O operation is in fact just copying of the data from / to the ring buffer, and thus is always synchronous since it completes quickly. I\u0027ve made a comment about that in state machines.",
